# What must never enter the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile copies seven explicit paths (app, static, skills, bootstrap,
# entrypoint.sh, scripts, docs/shipped-beads.jsonl). Everything below is either
# irrelevant to those or actively dangerous to walk.
#
# The dangerous one is `mnt/`. scripts/mount-kb.sh mounts the knowledge base
# there - usually the PRODUCTION database, since .env points at the same one the
# deployed machine uses. Without this file, `fly deploy` packs the build context
# by walking that mount: it reads the entire wiki out of Postgres over FUSE, and
# descends into TigerFS's control surface at `.schemas`, where an index
# directory contains itself. The walk does not terminate, the NFS server stalls
# ("nfs server 127.0.0.1:/: not responding"), and the deploy hangs before the
# image starts building. It also means the contents of the production knowledge
# base were being uploaded to the builder.
mnt/

# The Fly volume's local twin: the bead ledger, kb.git savepoint history and
# per-user scratch. Large, machine-local, and meaningless inside an image.
work/
work-dev/

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Secrets. Fly gets these as secrets, never baked into a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git/
.github/
.pre-commit-config.yaml
tests/
docs/decisions/
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.claude/

# Dolt/beads working files. .beads/issues.jsonl is committed, but nothing in
# the image reads it - the deployed ledger lives on the volume.
.beads/
.dolt/
*.db
*.gate.lock*
.beads-credential-key
